WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.532 --> 00:00:01.990
CARTER MORGAN:
Today, we're talking

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:05.470
about Workspace webinars, subsea
cables, the how and whys of

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:07.068
AI, and Ubuntu Pro.

00:00:07.068 --> 00:00:09.610
I'm Carter Morgan, and welcome
to "This Week in Cloud," where

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:12.942
we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:12.942 --> 00:00:14.900
Whether your team is
heading back to the office

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:16.970
or exploring a variety
of hybrid models,

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:19.687
Google Workspace will help you
adapt and make the most of it.

00:00:19.687 --> 00:00:22.020
Over the past year, we've
announced a variety of updates

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.080
to Google Workspace
from companion mode

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:25.760
to hybrid collaboration tools.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:28.010
Sign up for our free
upcoming webinar on July 28

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:29.930
to learn more.

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:32.299
Firmina, an open
subsea cable, will

00:00:32.299 --> 00:00:33.800
run from the East
Coast of the US

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.310
to Argentina, with additional
landings in Brazil and Uruguay.

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:38.780
Firmina will be
the longest cable

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:41.390
in the world capable of running
entirely from a single power

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:43.490
source at one end of the
cable if its other power

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:46.340
sources become temporarily
unavailable, a resilience boost

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:48.110
at a time when reliable
connectivity is

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:49.550
more important than ever.

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:51.920
Many companies today
are actively using AI

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:54.750
or have plans to incorporate it
into their future strategies.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:57.440
But as AI and advanced
analytics become more pervasive,

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:00.710
the need for more transparency
around how AI technology works

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:01.923
will be paramount.

00:01:01.923 --> 00:01:03.590
Decision-makers want
to know the reasons

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:06.020
behind an AI-based decision
so they have the confidence

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:07.130
that it's the right one.

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:09.620
Check out the blog to learn
more about why and how you

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:12.060
need to explain ML models.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:14.610
We're pleased to announce the
general availability of Ubuntu

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:17.250
Pro images on Google
Cloud, providing customers

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:19.800
with an improved Ubuntu
experience, expanded security

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:22.890
coverage, and integration with
critical Google Cloud features.

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:25.320
In partnership with Canonical,
we're making it even easier

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:28.170
for customers that have fully
embraced open source to ensure

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:29.760
security and compliance
for their most

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:32.197
mission-critical
enterprise workloads.

00:01:32.197 --> 00:01:34.280
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:36.150
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:38.570
Any thoughts or ideas, leave
us a comment or Tweet us,

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:41.020
and we'll see you in the Cloud.

